### DAY 9 EXERCISE 2: AUTHENTICATION TESTS
### ====================================================================

### 1. Register Success
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Aliyah",
  "email": "aliyah@company.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123"
}

###

### 2. Login Success
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@company.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123"
}

###

### 3. Duplicate Email Error
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Another Jane",
  "email": "jane.doe@company.com",
  "password": "DifferentPassword123"
}

###

### 4. Wrong Password Error
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@company.com",
  "password": "WrongPasswordAttempt"
}

### ====================================================================
### DAY 9 EXERCISE 3: ENDPOINT SECURITY TESTS
### ====================================================================

### 1. GET Tickets - No Token (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets

###

### 2. Register/Login as a USER to get a token
# @name userLogin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@company.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123"
}

### Store User Token
@userToken = {{userLogin.response.body.token}}

###

### 3. GET Tickets - With USER Token (Expected: 200 OK)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### 4. POST Ticket - With USER Token (Expected: 403 Forbidden)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Broken Keyboard",
  "description": "Keys are stuck",
  "category": "Hardware"
}

###

### 5. Register an Admin Account (Run once, adjust database directly if needed)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Admin User",
  "email": "admin@company.com",
  "password": "AdminPassword123"
}

# (Note: For testing ADMIN, manually/programmatically update admin@company.com's role to "ROLE_ADMIN" in MongoDB)

###

### 6. Login as ADMIN
# @name adminLogin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@company.com",
  "password": "AdminPassword123"
}

### Store Admin Token
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}

###

### 7. POST Ticket - With ADMIN Token (Expected: 201 Created / 200 OK)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Database Server Outage",
  "description": "Server is completely unresponsive.",
  "category": "Infrastructure",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "createdBy": "admin@company.com"
}